--- !tapi-tbd
# A hand-written stub for the seven CoreFoundation symbols `iana-time-zone`
# references on Apple targets (system timezone lookup, reached through
# chrono -> arrow-array -> parquet). It carries no Apple code: a `.tbd` is a
# symbol list, and the real framework is resolved from the system at run time
# through the install-name below.
#
# The release workflow cross-builds macOS binaries on Linux with cargo-zigbuild,
# and Zig ships stubs for libSystem only — without this the link fails with
# "unable to find framework 'CoreFoundation'". Adding a real Apple SDK would
# defeat the SDK-free design (see .github/workflows/release.yml).
tbd-version: 4
targets: [ x86_64-macos, arm64-macos ]
install-name: '/System/Library/Frameworks/CoreFoundation.framework/Versions/A/CoreFoundation'
# Deliberately LOW: dyld refuses to load a dylib whose compatibility version is
# older than the one recorded at link time, so claiming 1.0.0 always passes
# against the real framework (150.0.0 today) on every macOS version.
current-version: 1
compatibility-version: 1
exports:
  - targets: [ x86_64-macos, arm64-macos ]
    symbols:
      - _CFRelease
      - _CFStringGetBytes
      - _CFStringGetCStringPtr
      - _CFStringGetLength
      - _CFTimeZoneCopySystem
      - _CFTimeZoneGetName
      - _CFTimeZoneResetSystem
...
